WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.639
Vladimir Putin has set Russia on a
collision course with America and the

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:13.710
West. Putin sees Russians as heirs to a
vast empire; an empire they lost with the

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:17.369
fall of the Soviet Union. And the biggest
obstacle to their restored greatness? The

00:00:17.369 --> 00:00:22.560
United States. So Putin seeks to regain
control of the former Soviet states. He

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.130
wants to create a world in which the
US is just another country, rather than

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:31.320
a global leader. To that end, he's driving
a narrative that says, "If the US was just

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.850
cut down to size, Russia could regain its
empire and once again be the defender of

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.649
Europe and Christianity." In pursuit of
his vision, Putin is creating a Hobbesian

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:45.510
world of violence and lawlessness. His
seizure of Crimea was illegal. His

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:50.160
occupation of eastern Ukraine – again
illegal. Interference in US elections –

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.570
illegal. Cyber attacks on Baltic
countries – aggression. Deliberately

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:58.620
bombing hospitals in Syria – that's a war
crime. But Putin's Russia isn't the

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.110
Soviet Union. It's economy is the size of
Australia's. It's population is shrinking.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:06.680
We can resist Putin's aggression... and we
must.

